  "narration": [
    {
      "id": "world",
      "startFrame": 24,
      "endFrame": 476,
      "speed": 0.92,
      "text": "Welcome to ToyWorld: a living three-dimensional road network built from real streets in Pune. Twenty junctions form a compact world where autonomous agents can navigate, make choices, and reveal how they reason."
    },
    {
      "id": "problem",
      "startFrame": 488,
      "endFrame": 908,
      "speed": 0.92,
      "text": "The problem is simple. Most AI observability tells us that a request happened, how long it took, and how many tokens it used. It still cannot tell us whether the decision was correct, or worth its cost."
    },
    {
      "id": "experiment",
      "startFrame": 920,
      "endFrame": 1379,
      "speed": 0.94,
      "text": "ToyWorld turns that missing signal into a controlled experiment. Seven language models face the same journeys and produce four hundred and twenty decisions across route choice, arrival-time estimation, and the next road to take."
    },
    {
      "id": "language",
      "startFrame": 1391,
      "endFrame": 1827,
      "speed": 0.94,
      "text": "Each color represents a different model moving through the same environment. Correct routes resolve in green. Wrong answers resolve in red, while the yellow ghost shows the optimal alternative the agent could have chosen."
    },
    {
      "id": "decision",
      "startFrame": 1839,
      "endFrame": 2285,
      "speed": 0.93,
      "text": "Follow one agent and every choice becomes inspectable: the question it received, its selected path, the known correct answer, its token usage, price, difficulty, and whether the journey later succeeded in reality."
    },
    {
      "id": "gradebook",
      "startFrame": 2297,
      "endFrame": 2726,
      "speed": 0.94,
      "text": "Gradebook captures that evidence as standard OpenTelemetry evaluation data. It records the source of truth, prices the decision, and links later real-world outcomes back to the exact choice that caused them."
    },
    {
      "id": "results",
      "startFrame": 2738,
      "endFrame": 3151,
      "speed": 0.93,
      "text": "Now the run has an honest result: two hundred and sixty-eight correct decisions, one hundred and forty observed outcomes, forty cents in total cost, and a measurable cost for every correct decision."
    },
    {
      "id": "broader",
      "startFrame": 3163,
      "endFrame": 3580,
      "speed": 0.96,
      "text": "ToyWorld makes the idea visible, but Gradebook is built for any AI system. When a decision has a deterministic check or an observable outcome, performance stops being an assertion and becomes evidence."
    }
  ],
